+/// Whether `raw` is shaped like something [`resolve`] could take — a uid or a label —
+/// without needing the store to say so.
+///
+/// `trace`'s uid positional became optional; its store positional did not move. A single
+/// bare argument still fills the first positional, so `smysl trace some-store.smy` would
+/// otherwise be read as a (doomed) attempt to trace the label `some-store.smy`. The same
+/// syntax [`resolve`] uses to tell a uid from a label — `b3:…` versus never containing `:`
+/// — also tells either of them from a path, so a lone argument that is neither is read as
+/// the store instead.
+fn looks_like_unit_ref(raw: &str) -> bool {
+    smysl::Label::new(raw).is_ok() || UidPrefix::parse(raw).is_ok()
+}
